{red|**Reflect honestly on your current approach to discipline.**

Where do you fall on the harsh to permissive spectrum?}{red| Where does your spouse fall?}{red| What specific discipline approaches do you disagree about?}{red| When you disagree, what usually happens?}{red| Are your children getting consistent or inconsistent messages about consequences?}

Write your honest assessment of discipline in your home:

{red|**Honestly assess how well you are protecting your marriage during these parenting years.**

How often do you have dedicated couple time?}{red| When did you last have a conversation that was not about children or logistics?}{red| How is your physical intimacy?}{red| Do you feel like partners or just co-parents?}{red| What is your marriage getting that children's activities are not taking?}

Write your honest assessment:

{red|**Honestly assess exhaustion in your family right now.**

How depleted are you?}{red| How depleted is your spouse?}{red| How is exhaustion affecting your marriage?}{red| What rest are you each getting, and is it enough?}{red| What could change to build more rest into your life?}

Write your assessment:

{red|**Together, create a plan for managing exhaustion and building rest into your life.**

**Schedule regular breaks for each parent.** Decide what is realistic given your circumstances.

**Identify one thing you can cut or outsource to reduce the load.**

**Discuss how you will support each other when one of you is depleted.** What signals will you watch for?}{red| What support will you provide?}

{red|**Remember that rest is not selfish.** It is how you sustain the energy to be good parents and good spouses over the long haul.

What specific steps will you take to manage exhaustion?}

{red|**Reflect on the parenting stage you are currently in.**

What are the unique challenges of this stage?}{red| How is this stage affecting your marriage specifically?}{red| What do you and your spouse need from each other right now?}{red| How well are you supporting each other through this stage's demands?}

Write about your current stage and its impact:

{red|What is the most important thing you learned about parenting as partners through this journey?}

{red|What do you want to remember when parenting gets hard and you are tempted to turn on each other instead of toward each other?}

Write your greatest insight:

{red|Based on this journey, what specific changes will you make to how you parent together?}

